root.innerHTML=`<header><div><div class="eyebrow">FLYKART / LEARNING JOURNEY · STAGE 04</div><h1>Parking simulator<span class="tag">.</span></h1></div><nav><a href="./index.html">1 · Racer</a><a href="./vision.html#track">2 · Vision</a><a href="./vision.html#world">3 · Explore</a><a href="./robot.html">5 · 3D habitat</a><a href="./robot.html#calibration-panel">6 · Calibration</a></nav></header>
<main><div class="toolbar"><button id="run" class="primary">▶ Run fly</button><button id="step">Step 1 s</button><button id="reset">Replay lot</button><button id="new-lot">New random lot</button><label>Lesson<select id="lesson">${LESSONS.map(l=>`<option value="${l.id}">${l.title}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label>Drive<select id="drive"><option value="fly">Neural fly</option><option value="manual">Manual · WASD / arrows</option></select></label><label class="check"><input id="sonar-on" type="checkbox" checked> Sonar on</label><label>Speed<select id="speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="4">4×</option><option value="16">16×</option><option value="0">Maximum</option></select></label></div>
<div class="card import-panel"><div class="row"><b>Load a brain</b><button id="brain-upload" class="primary">Import / paste brain…</button><input id="import-brain" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"><button id="export-brain">Export fly + eyes</button><button id="adapt-racer" disabled>Adapt racer parent to parking</button><span id="brain-name" class="help">Loading world eyes…</span></div><div id="brain-shelf"></div></div>
<section class="card training-card training-top"><div class="training-setup"><h2>Train parking controller offspring</h2><div class="fields"><label>Generations<input id="generations" type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="3"></label><label>Ghosts / generation<input id="population" type="number" min="2" max="32" value="6"></label><label>Training speed<select id="training-speed"><option value="0">Maximum · CPU limited</option><option value="256">256×</option><option value="64">64×</option><option value="16">16×</option><option value="4">4×</option><option value="1">1× · watch</option></select></label><label>Mutation run seed<input id="training-seed" type="number" min="1" max="999999999" value="7331"></label></div></div><div id="training-runtime-controls" class="training-runtime"><button id="headless-evolve" class="primary">Start headless evolution</button><button id="watch-now">View now</button><button id="headless-again">Go headless</button><details><summary>Inspect selected generations</summary><div class="runtime-schedule"><label>View run generation · 0 = off<input id="watch-generation" type="number" min="0" max="1000" value="0"></label><label>View every N generations · 0 = off<input id="watch-every" type="number" min="0" max="1000" value="0"></label><label>Speed while auto-watching<select id="watch-speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="4" selected>4×</option><option value="16">16×</option><option value="64">64×</option></select></label></div><small>Views turn on for the selected generation, then return to headless. These are generation numbers within this run; 0 (held-out tests) remains headless. Change the schedule during training.</small></details><small id="training-runtime-note" role="status"></small><div id="training-processes" class="training-processes" role="status"></div></div><div class="row actions"><button id="evolve" class="primary">Evolve ghosts</button><button id="cancel" disabled>Cancel</button><button id="adopt" disabled>Use tested offspring</button><button id="export-report" disabled>Export run report</button></div><div class="progress"><div id="training-progress"></div></div><p id="training-status" class="status">Completed generation winners autosave as the next evolution parent. Live driving changes when you use tested offspring.</p><details class="training-options"><summary>Rehearsal lessons, breeding objective & manual coaching</summary><label>Breed for <select id="selection"><option value="score">Reward / task score · default</option><option value="speed">Progress per second</option><option value="safety">Fewest crashes per progress</option><option value="balanced">Balanced · custom weights</option></select></label><div class="fields breeding-weights"><label>Score weight<input id="score-weight" type="number" min="0" max="1" step=".1" value=".5"></label><label>Speed weight<input id="speed-weight" type="number" min="0" max="1" step=".1" value=".3"></label><label>Safety weight<input id="safety-weight" type="number" min="0" max="1" step=".1" value=".2"></label></div><small class="help">Weights apply to Balanced only and are normalized. Completed parking remains dominant; zero-chill rejects collisions as before. Speed means distance progress per elapsed second. Safety means contacts per useful progress, so standing still cannot win. Held-out tests use this same objective.</small><div class="lesson-list" id="curriculum">${LESSONS.map(l=>`<label><input type="checkbox" value="${l.id}"${EASY_PARKING_LESSONS.includes(l.id)?' checked':''}>${l.title.slice(5)}</label>`).join('')}</div><small class="help">Always train the active lesson plus a rotating selected lesson on fresh common seeds. Defaults rehearse finding, leaving and switching bays. Precise/parallel/traffic lessons are opt-in. Every ghost has its own world. Earlier skills are tested before adoption; ghosts cannot block one another.</small><details><summary>Teach from your own driving</summary><label class="check"><input id="record-coach" type="checkbox"> Record manual sensor/action examples</label><label class="check"><input id="use-coach" type="checkbox"> Seed one child from those examples</label><small id="coach-info">0 manual examples · capped at 2,000. Other ghosts preserve the parent. Held-out tests still gate adoption.</small></details></details></section>
<div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><b id="quality">0%</b><small>Parking quality · external judge</small></div><div class="metric"><b id="reward">0.0</b><small id="reward-note">Sugar / reward · training only</small></div><div class="metric"><b id="pain">0.0</b><small>Impact + visual-stall pain</small></div><div class="metric"><b id="completion">Searching</b><small id="completion-note">Fit → stop → hold 1 second</small></div></div>
<div class="layout"><section class="card world"><div class="world-head"><b id="lot-title">3D / PARKING LOT</b><div class="row"><select id="lot-view" aria-label="Parking lot view"><option value="3d">3D · orbit & zoom</option><option value="plan">Top plan · low CPU</option></select><button id="view-fit">Fit lot</button><button id="view-close">Close view</button></div><span id="run-info">Paused</span></div><canvas id="lot-3d" width="1000" height="600" aria-label="Solid 3D parking blocks, car bodies and pedestrians"></canvas><canvas id="lot" hidden width="1000" height="600" aria-label="Parking lot, bays, moving traffic, pedestrians and independent ghost cars"></canvas><div class="world-foot"><div class="ghost-picker"><label>Inspect cart <select id="inspect-ghost" disabled><option value="0">Live robot</option></select></label><small id="ghost-inspection-note">Click a coloured ghost during evolution to inspect its own camera, sonar and controls.</small></div><p id="motion-judge-status" class="judge-status" role="status"></p><small id="sensor-agreement"></small><div id="sensor-badges" class="sensor-badges" aria-label="Active driver and sensors"></div><div class="control-display"><label class="check"><input id="show-controls" type="checkbox" checked> Show control requests</label><small id="control-source"></small><div id="control-outputs" class="control-outputs">${[['forward','↑ Forward'],['reverse','↓ Reverse'],['left','← Left'],['right','Right →'],['brake','Brake'],['stop','Stop']].map(([id,label])=>`<output id="control-${id}" data-control="${id}">${label}<b>0%</b></output>`).join('')}</div></div><small class="help ghost-isolation">Coloured training ghosts are comparison overlays only: they cannot see, sense, collide with, or yield to each other. Each has its own lot. Grey vehicles are real obstacles; moving traffic appears only in the Traffic lesson.</small><small id="goal-cue-status" class="help" role="status"></small><small id="sensor-audit" class="help"></small><div class="row"><button id="save-state">Save replay lot + brain + memory</button><button id="load-state">Import / paste state…</button><input id="import-state" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"><button id="export-3d">Export 3D scene</button><a href="./robot.html">Open 3D ↗</a></div><small>Pink flag + yellow area mark the target. Direction paint is off unless explicitly enabled for orientation training. Click a vacant bay to practise there. Solid blocks have the robot’s footprint and 11 cm height. Drag to orbit; scroll/pinch to zoom. Car bodies keep the same contact footprint.</small><div id="manual-pad" class="row" hidden><button data-drive="w">↑ Forward</button><button data-drive="a">← Left</button><button id="manual-stop">Stop</button><button data-drive="d">Right →</button><button data-drive="s">↓ Reverse</button><small>Hold a button to drive. Steering works with forward or reverse.</small></div><label class="check"><input id="trail" type="checkbox" checked> Show crayon driving history</label><p id="status" class="status" role="status">Loading…</p></div></section>
<aside class="monitors"><section class="card monitor"><h2>01 / FPV CAMERA <span id="camera-size"></span></h2><canvas id="camera" width="480" height="240" aria-label="Actual low resolution RGB camera pixels"></canvas><small>Actual inference capture, enlarged with nearest-neighbour pixels. Colour; capture follows the selected camera mount.</small></section><section id="eye-monitor" class="card monitor"><h2>02 / FLY EYES · SWARM CROPS</h2><canvas id="eyes" width="480" height="240" aria-label="Actual filtered crop inputs for every fly eye"></canvas><small id="eye-info">Central eye</small><div id="spikes" class="neural"></div></section><section class="card monitor"><h2>03 / SCAN MEMORY · SONAR GROUND MAP</h2><canvas id="scan" width="480" height="280" aria-label="Sonar return evidence ground map"></canvas><div class="monitor-buttons"><button id="scan-view">Perspective / top</button><button id="clear-scan">Clear scan</button><label class="scan-overlay-toggle"><input id="parking-scan-reference" type="checkbox"> Scene overlay</label><label>Evidence<select id="scan-evidence"><option value="arcs">Echo uncertainty arcs</option><option value="cells">Legacy coarse cells</option></select></label><label class="scan-overlay-toggle"><input id="scan-transmission" type="checkbox" checked> Simulated transmission fan</label><details class="scan-settings"><summary>Filter & opacity</summary>${scanComparisonControls('parking-scan',true)}</details></div><div class="scan-zoom-controls"><button id="scan-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom sonar map out">−</button><output id="scan-zoom-level">1×</output><button id="scan-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom sonar map in">＋</button><button id="scan-fit">Fit lot</button><button id="scan-follow">Follow cart</button><small>Wheel to zoom · drag to pan</small></div><small id="sonar-info">HC-SR04 · ~15 Hz · no echo means unknown. Map is a diagnostic, excluded from neural inputs.</small></section></aside></div>
<div class="controls"><section class="card"><h2>Lesson & objective</h2><p id="lesson-help" class="help"></p><div class="fields"><label>Goal cue<select id="cue"><option value="visual">Explore · camera only target</option><option value="compass">Explicit goal compass</option></select></label><label>Learning phase<select id="phase"><option value="shaped">Guided · distance + quality sugar</option><option value="sparse">Sparse · completed parking sugar</option><option value="frozen">Frozen · no sugar / no learning</option></select></label><label>Seed<input id="seed" type="number" min="1" max="999999999"></label><label>Episode time · seconds<input id="seconds" type="number" min="2" max="180" value="30"></label><label>Crash priority <output id="crash-label">20%</output><input id="crash-weight" type="range" min="0" max="1" step=".05" value=".2"></label><label>Arrival criteria<select id="criteria" disabled><option>Entire body + orientation + stop</option></select></label></div><label class="check"><input id="strict-crash" type="checkbox"> Zero chill · eradicate crashes & futile motion</label><small class="help">An outside-bay collision, 2 seconds of confirmed pointless rocking, or prolonged no-progress with less than 4 cm net movement in the observation window ends and disqualifies the trial. The eradicator adds pain and negative reward, removes that ghost from the view, and records its reason. Valid stopped parking/reward holds are exempt. Every failed candidate is excluded from breeding; the saved parent is kept if all fail.</small><label class="delay-field">Eradicator · no-progress limit / seconds<input id="eradicator-seconds" type="number" min="4" max="60" step="1" value="12"></label><small class="help">Active only with Zero chill. Moving explorers can continue; wheel commands without net body progress do not reset this limit. Camera-only search has no judge coordinates in its neural inputs.</small><label class="check"><input id="delay-reward" type="checkbox"> Delayed sugar · require controls released</label><label class="delay-field">Extra reward delay · seconds<input id="reward-delay" type="number" min=".25" max="10" step=".25" value="2" disabled></label><small class="help">When checked, all sugar waits for valid parking, one second stopped, then this extra delay with throttle, reverse, steering and brake released (≤3% deadband). Moving, contact or pressing a control resets the wait. Pending sugar is lost on timeout. Training ghosts follow the same rule.</small><small class="help">Loose lessons allow 27 cm centre tolerance and any direction, but still require stopping. Precise lessons require the full chassis inside the square, heading within 15°, and a contact-free one-second hold. Seeing the flag never wins.</small></section>
<section class="card reward-coach"><h2>Reward coach · training judge</h2><label class="check"><input id="pain-and-penalty" type="checkbox"> Pain + negative reward together</label><label class="delay-field">Negative reward per pain unit<input id="pain-reward-weight" type="number" min=".1" max="10" step=".1" value="1"></label><small class="help">Mirrors collision, slow-driving and sensor-stall pain into immediate negative sugar as well as the usual pain-weighted score. Reward delay holds positive bonuses only. Frozen tests record negative feedback in the score without dispensing sugar. These are external evolution labels; no pain or hidden goal input is added to the brain.</small><label class="check"><input id="anti-jiggle" type="checkbox" checked> Penalize repeated forward / reverse without progress</label><div class="fields"><label>Observation window · seconds<input id="jiggle-window" type="number" min="2" max="10" step=".5" value="4"></label><label>Jiggle pain · units/second<input id="jiggle-weight" type="number" min=".1" max="10" step=".1" value="2"></label></div><small class="help">Four meaningful direction changes in this window, with no new 2 cm goal/route progress or useful final alignment, trigger both pain and negative reward. Actual legs must move 1.2 cm; sustained alternating motor requests also detect rocking against a solid object. Useful reversing and valid parking holds are exempt. Costs rise while the oscillation continues, capped at 10 pain/s.</small><label class="check"><input id="approach-reward" type="checkbox" checked> Reward approaching the parking space</label><label class="delay-field">Approach radius · metres<input id="approach-radius" type="number" min=".5" max="6" step=".25" value="3"></label><small class="help">Inside this radius, moving closer adds sugar; moving away subtracts it. Returning to the same position cancels approach sugar. Parking alignment has its own signed reward.</small><label class="check"><input id="progress-penalty" type="checkbox" checked> Penalize no useful progress</label><small class="help">After 3 seconds without a new 2 cm improvement (or useful final alignment), the score loses 1 point/s, doubling every 3 seconds up to 10/s. Loops and spinning wheels do not reset it. Valid parking and the reward delay are exempt.</small><label class="check"><input id="reverse-reward" type="checkbox"> Extra sugar for useful reverse</label><small class="help">Actual backward movement must improve the best goal distance, or advance the coach route. Up to 5 extra sugar per episode; backing against a wall or repeating a loop earns none.</small><label class="check"><input id="path-reward" type="checkbox"> Path coach · reward following a planned route</label><small class="help">A geometry-aware planner searches forward and reverse curves with 18 cm minimum turning radius, checking the swept 26 × 17 cm chassis with clearance. It favours gentle turns and fewer direction changes; costly pivots remain possible for this skid-steer robot. This bounded search gives a feasible guide, not guaranteed global optimality. Following it gives signed progress sugar and leaving it reduces sugar. Moving traffic still needs sensor-based avoidance. If planning fails, route rewards stay off.</small><label class="check"><input id="slow-driving" type="checkbox"> Penalize crawling outside the target parking area</label><div class="fields"><label>Slow-driving feedback<select id="slow-mode"><option value="penalty">Score penalty</option><option value="pain">Pain signal</option><option value="both">Pain + negative reward</option></select></label><label>Minimum travel speed · cm/s<input id="slow-speed" type="number" min="1" max="30" step="1" value="5"></label><label>Slow cost · units/second<input id="slow-weight" type="number" min=".1" max="10" step=".1" value="1"></label><label>Safe manoeuvring radius · m<input id="slow-zone" type="number" min=".27" max="2" step=".05" value=".45"></label></div><small class="help">Optional: after a 1-second start grace, actual travel below this speed loses score or adds pain, scaled by the speed shortfall. Forward and reverse count equally. Inside the target safe radius, slow precision parking and waiting are exempt. Wheel commands without body movement still count as slow. This external training judge adds no hidden speed/goal input to the fly.</small><label class="check"><input id="show-coach" type="checkbox" checked> Show radius rings & coach route in lot</label><small id="path-coach-info" class="help" role="status">Path coach off.</small><div id="reward-breakdown" class="reward-breakdown" role="status"></div><small class="help">Approach, reverse and route sugar apply in Guided mode. Sparse rewards completed parking only; Frozen gives no sugar. Delayed sugar holds every bonus until success. No-progress penalties apply to the evaluation score in every phase. Rings, route and judge coordinates never enter the camera or neural inputs. The route planner is training-only supervision; switch it off before testing independent exploration.</small></section><section class="card"><h2>Eyes, memory & traffic</h2><details><summary>Robot motors · forward & reverse speed</summary><div class="fields"><label>Nominal wheel RPM at 6 V<input id="motor-rpm" type="number" min="100" max="240" value="180"></label><label>Supply voltage · V<input id="motor-voltage" type="number" min="3" max="9" step=".1" value="6"></label><label>Driver voltage loss · V<input id="motor-drop" type="number" min="0" max="4" step=".1" value="1.8"></label><label>Reverse speed fraction<input id="motor-reverse" type="number" min=".3" max="1" step=".05" value="1"></label></div><small id="motor-info" class="help"></small><small class="help">65 mm wheels, 48:1 motors. 100–240 RPM gives 0.34–0.82 m/s at the wheel before driver/load losses. Both directions use the same motor model by default. Speed scales with estimated motor voltage; keep it ≤6 V. Motor response is 0.16 s, with PWM deadband and skid/slip. These are simulation assumptions: measure straight, reverse and turning speed on the real cart. Training speed only accelerates the simulation clock.</small></details><div class="fields"><label>Lot difficulty<select id="parking-layout"><option value="standard">Standard · wide aisle</option><option value="tight">Tight · closer neighbours</option><option value="angled">Angled · diagonal bays</option><option value="double-row">Double row · opposing parked cars</option></select></label><label>Floor appearance<select id="floor"><option value="transfer">Transfer grass · open-world eyes</option><option value="asphalt">Asphalt · parking adaptation</option></select></label><label>Camera mount<select id="camera-mount"><option value="trained">Keep imported eye camera</option><option value="robot">Robot sensor head · 6.5 cm</option></select></label><label>Virtual fly eyes<select id="swarm"><option value="single">1 · central</option><option value="circle3">3 · crop ensemble</option><option value="circle5">5 · crop ensemble</option><option value="circle9">9 · crop ensemble</option><option value="scales3">3 · zoom scales</option></select></label><label class="check"><input id="memory-on" type="checkbox" checked>Kenyon visual recall</label><small class="memory-cost-help">CPU cost scales with cell count for every ghost. Turn recall off for camera + sonar only, or choose 512 cells for faster memory experiments. Memory stays stored; off runs do not read or train it.</small><label>Kenyon visual cells<select id="memory-size">${MEMORY_SIZES.map(n=>`<option value="${n}"${n===4096?' selected':''}>${n.toLocaleString()}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><label>Moving vehicles<input id="traffic-count" type="number" min="0" max="8" value="3"></label><label>Walking pedestrians<input id="pedestrian-count" type="number" min="0" max="8" value="2"></label><label>Rendering / CPU<select id="preview"><option value="full">Full preview</option><option value="low">Low CPU · 5 fps</option><option value="headless">Headless · fast training</option></select></label><button id="refresh">Refresh views once</button></div><small class="help">Transfer grass keeps the familiar open-world ground texture. Asphalt can look like obstacles to grass-trained eyes; adapt the camera network before switching. Keep the trained eye’s height, field of view and pitch for parent transfer. The robot head changes the view and needs camera adaptation. Sonar stays at the physical 6.5 cm height; off supplies zero sonar inputs and pauses scan recording.</small><label class="check"><input id="gap-hints" type="checkbox" checked> Chassis-aware camera hints · inputs 15/16</label><small class="help">Uses only the nine camera clearance estimates and motor speed estimate, with the 17 cm body width and a short speed-dependent look-ahead. Flanking cars outside the body corridor no longer make the whole row a wall. Switch off for the inherited World hint formula; raw camera estimates and sonar channels remain unchanged. Older saved parking setups keep the legacy formula until enabled. These are fallible sensor-derived hints, not a safety controller.</small><label class="check"><input id="bay-practice" type="checkbox"> Centered bay entry / straight-back exit practice</label><small class="help">Arrival starts 0.8–1.2 m in front of the vacant bay with small seeded offsets. Exit puts the flag nearly straight behind the nose-in robot. Both use normal camera/sonar and existing success rules; no hidden target cue is added. Mix regular lots afterward to avoid learning one manoeuvre only. Optional reverse sugar below rewards useful reverse progress.</small><label class="check"><input id="bay-alignment" type="checkbox"> Visible direction paint + bay advisory · opt-in</label><small class="help">Off by default: no blue/orange paint appears in the camera or lot. Enable only for precise orientation lessons: paint enters RGB and input 15 gets the observed direction. The patches are flat paint, never sonar targets or collision bodies. Imported open-world eyes may misread unfamiliar paint; adapt and test before using it.</small><label class="check"><input id="remember" type="checkbox"> Keep visual world memory between live runs</label><label class="check"><input id="cars" type="checkbox"> Replace blocks with car skins</label><label class="check"><input id="parked-offset" type="checkbox"> Imperfect parking · ±3 cm on each axis / 10° yaw</label><small class="help">Seeded real body offsets; camera, sonar and contacts use the same geometry. Vacant start and target spaces remain clear. Lot difficulty applies to every training and held-out scene.</small><label class="check"><input id="jitter" type="checkbox"> Small seeded vehicle-size variations (±4%)</label><label class="check"><input id="normalize" type="checkbox"> Normalize camera contrast</label><button id="forget">Forget visual memory</button><small id="memory-info" class="help">4,096 sparse visual cells. Crops share one physical camera; they are not extra physical viewpoints.</small><small class="help">Traffic lesson: one clockwise lane, following headway, pedestrian priority and parking-yield rules. Walkers visit parked cars; those cars then leave. This is an illustrative traffic model.</small></section>
</div>
<details class="card input-audit"><summary>What reaches the fly · transfer & scoring</summary><small>Camera → frozen world vision CNN → clearance estimates; processed RGB → flag bearing/apparent size and two-colour ground-marker direction; HC-SR04 → closeness/strength; body → motor-model speed estimate and last motor requests. Visual mode supplies zero target cue while unseen and never reads target position or compass. Compass mode explicitly uses relative target bearing, distance and heading. The chassis-aware option changes derived camera hints 15/16 using estimated ranges and robot width; the legacy World formula remains available. Neither reads the scan map or scene geometry. The optional bay-direction setting adds observed alignment only in precise lessons. Pose, crash labels, parking quality, rewards and scan map are external labels, never neural inputs. The inherited CNN was not trained on these lots; measure held-out performance.</small><small>Shaped sugar is a signed change in a distance/quality potential, so driving in circles cannot farm positive rewards. Sparse mode rewards completed parking only. Frozen mode pauses learning and sugar, retaining collision penalties. Pedestrian contact ends the episode; the animation does not alter observations or scores.</small><small>Export fly + eyes imports through Vision and 3D. Save browser brain keeps a separate Parking checkpoint; choose Parking simulator in the 3D browser shelf. Export 3D scene transfers static geometry and a sugar target; its basic sugar judge does not enforce parking containment/orientation. Moving traffic is frozen in that scene. Parking input advisory and renderers differ, so test/retrain before physical use.</small></details>
<section class="card logs"><div class="row"><h2>Sensor & training console</h2><div class="row"><button id="copy-logs">Copy logs · one click</button><button id="save-logs">Save logs</button><button id="clear-logs">Clear</button></div></div><pre id="logs" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copyable sensor and training logs"></pre></section><footer><a href="https://github.com/nomsams/flykart/blob/main/docs/parking-simulator.md">Teaching & transfer guide ↗</a> · Racer → Vision → Explore world → Parking → 3D habitat → Real-world calibration.</footer></main>`;

let plots:ParkingPlots,plotBase=0,selectedGhost=0;
function observedSession(){return ghosts[selectedGhost]??ghosts[0]??session;}
